GARDEN PLANNER CHANGE LOG
=========================
Newest entries first. Each entry lists what was Added, Changed, Fixed, or Removed,
plus any Notes (things to know before deploying or testing).

This log was started on 2026-10-09. Entries for earlier versions were reconstructed
from the project history and have no exact dates.

Update rule: every change to the app gets an entry here, and package.json's
"version" is bumped to match.


[2.0.0] 2026-10-09  Phase 2 photo galleries
-------------------------------------------
Added
- Multiple photos per plant, stored in Vercel Blob (api/photo.js uploads a full-size
  photo and a thumbnail, and deletes them on request).
- Photo gallery viewer: tap a plant thumbnail (plant card or calendar) to see an enlarged
  photo inside the app, with previous/next buttons, arrow keys, and Escape to close.
- Photo order setting: Timeline (oldest first) or By season, which ignores the year and
  groups spring, summer, autumn, and winter (meteorological seasons, flipped for the
  southern hemisphere). Available in Settings > Photos and in the gallery.
- Per-photo date (defaults to the file's date), caption, set-as-cover, and delete.
- Duplicate identification prompt now offers "Add photo to this plant".
- "+" tile on plants without photos opens the gallery to add one; a count badge shows
  how many photos a plant has.

Changed
- Photos found by identification are saved immediately as a small copy and uploaded to
  Blob in the background, so adding a plant is not delayed.
- Deleting a plant also deletes its stored photos.
- Cloud sync and backups now carry photo lists (links, dates, captions), and photo URLs
  are validated on load (only Blob links and embedded JPEGs are accepted).
- package.json version 2.0.0; added dependency @vercel/blob.

Removed
- "Replace photo" in the duplicate prompt (replaced by adding to the gallery).

Notes
- Requires a Public Blob store connected to the project (provides BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN).
  Photo links are unguessable but not password protected.
- Older single photos become the first gallery photo and stay small (about 320 px).
- If upload fails, the gallery offers to keep a small copy inside the garden data.
- Tested against a stand-in for Blob, not the live service.


[1.4.0] 2026-10-09  Phase 1 identification workflow
---------------------------------------------------
Changed
- "Add to my plants" now saves the plant immediately (photo, names, tasks, notes)
  instead of filling in the manual form. A confirmation shows spot checkboxes
  ("Where is it growing?") and an Undo button.
- Low-confidence identifications show "Add anyway" plus a note suggesting a clearer photo.
- Scientific name is now shown in bold italics with the common name beside it, on
  plant cards, the calendar, the focus list, and the spots list.
- Tapping a "could also be" suggestion now switches the species on the current result,
  keeps the photo, and uses a care lookup. It does not call Plant.id again.
- Hourly identification limit lowered from 20 to 10 per IP (care lookups stay at 40).

Added
- Short care notes (sun, soil, water, one tip) for all 51 built-in species, used
  automatically so notes always transfer for those plants.
- Edit button on each plant card: edit common name, scientific name, and notes.
- Duplicate check: if an identified species matches a saved plant (by scientific name,
  or genus when either side is "spp."), the user chooses to replace that plant's photo
  or add it as a new plant.
- Small plant thumbnail next to tasks in the calendar month list and the 30-day focus list.
- Message when a care lookup fails, saying generic tasks will be used.
- Same-photo retries in one session reuse the earlier result (no extra Plant.id credit).
- Specific error message when a photo format cannot be read (for example iPhone HEIC).
- Alert when browser storage is full, so failed saves are no longer silent.

Fixed
- Photo was dropped when a "could also be" suggestion was tapped.
- Care notes were blank for species already in the built-in list.
- Plant.id results with no common name showed the scientific name in the common-name slot.
- Plant IDs could collide if two plants were created within the same millisecond.

Notes
- Each plant still has a single photo. "Replace photo" overwrites it. Multiple photos per
  plant are planned for Phase 2.
- Existing plants get their scientific name filled in automatically when they belong to
  a built-in species. Plants typed by hand can be updated with the Edit button.


[1.3.0] Cloud sync
------------------
Added
- Cross-device sync: api/garden.js stores the whole garden as one JSON row in Postgres
  (Neon). Uses the same password as photo identification.
- Versioned saves with conflict handling: a second device editing the same version is
  asked whether to keep its own copy or use the cloud copy.
- Sync status line at the top of the app (Synced, Syncing, Offline, Sync off).
- Settings > Backup: download and restore the garden as a JSON file.
- Local-first behavior: changes save in the browser first and upload shortly after.

Changed
- Data from backups and the cloud is sanitized on load (ids, photo data, task names,
  numeric fields), and calendar reasons are escaped.
- package.json now depends on @neondatabase/serverless.

Notes
- Requires the Neon integration (Vercel Storage tab), which provides DATABASE_URL.
- One shared garden per password. Sync only works on the Vercel deployment.


[1.2.0] Manual care lookup
--------------------------
Added
- "Look up care for this name" button in the manual add form for plants not in the
  built-in list. Claude resolves common or scientific names and returns type,
  hardiness range, tasks with priorities, notes, and toxicity.
- Species learned this way are saved so each is looked up only once.
- Manual form relabeled "Add a plant manually".

Changed
- api/care.js also returns recognized, common, and scientific fields.


[1.1.0] Hybrid identification
-----------------------------
Added
- Plant.id integration for photo identification (probability, alternatives, optional
  health check). Claude supplies care tasks only for species not already known.
- IDENTIFIER=claude setting to compare against Claude-only identification.
- api/care.js (text-only Claude lookup), api/_lib.js (shared password, rate limit,
  validation helpers). Models set by CLAUDE_MODEL and CARE_MODEL.

Notes
- Needs PLANT_ID_API_KEY and ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. Plant.id request details were based on
  published examples and should be checked against their current docs if requests fail.


[1.0.0] First Vercel package
----------------------------
Added
- Project folder for Vercel: index.html, api/identify.js, vercel.json, package.json.
- Photo identification through Claude vision, with the API key kept on the server.
- Shared-password protection, image size cap, per-IP rate limit, and validated output.
- Browser-side photo resizing (1024 px) and small thumbnails saved with each plant.


[0.4.0] Lavender pruning
------------------------
Changed
- Lavender uses a species-specific task, "Prune before frost", scheduled about 6 weeks
  before the first frost, and existing lavender plants were migrated to it.


[0.3.0] Garden spots
--------------------
Added
- Spots tab: create garden spots and set sunlight (full sun, part sun, part shade,
  full shade). Each spot lists its plants.
- Plants can belong to several spots (checkboxes replaced the original dropdown).
- Older single-spot text was converted into spots automatically.


[0.2.0] Plant database and priorities
-------------------------------------
Added
- Built-in list of about 50 common garden plants with autocomplete by common or
  scientific name.
- Annual vs perennial status by hardiness zone, with tasks adjusted for plants grown
  as annuals in the user's zone.
- Task priorities (Critical, Recommended, Optional) and a "Focus for the next 30 days"
  list ranked by importance and urgency, with a plant-health reason for each task.


[0.1.0] Initial planner
-----------------------
Added
- Plant catalogue with care tasks (heavy and light pruning, deadheading, fertilizing,
  dividing, cutting back for winter).
- Month calendar of tasks scheduled from the user's last spring and first fall frost
  dates, with a USDA zone selector and editable frost dates.
- Local browser storage and tick-off of completed tasks.


PLANNED
-------
- Plant recommendations by spot sunlight and desired traits (height, ground cover,
  bloom season, flower and leaf color).
- Treatment text for Plant.id health checks.
- Stricter rate limiting backed by a data store.
